<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Elena Ceaușescu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1916–1989</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Elena Ceaușescu (1916–1989) was the wife of the Romanian communist leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nicolae-ceausescu">Nicolae Ceaușescu</a> and from the 1970s the second most powerful person in the country, as a member of the party's top body and first deputy prime minister. Despite little formal schooling she was promoted as a world-renowned chemist. She was tried with her husband by a military tribunal and executed with him on 25 December 1989.</p></div>
